An integrated Indian agri-processing company running sugar, ethanol/distillery and co-generation power operations across Punjab and Uttar Pradesh.","business":"Rana Sugars Limited manufactures crystal sugar, ethanol/spirit and co-generated power through three integrated manufacturing facilities in Uttar Pradesh (Moradabad, Rampur) and Punjab (Amritsar). It pioneered sugar-beet-based sugar manufacturing in India alongside conventional cane crushing, and its distillery can run on molasses, sugarcane juice/syrup or grains, including production of Extra Neutral Alcohol (ENA)."},"products":[],"endMarkets":"Domestic Indian sugar market|Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) programme / Oil Marketing Companies|Punjab|Uttar Pradesh","currentContext":{"business":"Rana Sugars Limited manufactures crystal sugar, ethanol/spirit and co-generated power through three integrated manufacturing facilities in Uttar Pradesh (Moradabad, Rampur) and Punjab (Amritsar). It pioneered sugar-beet-based sugar manufacturing in India alongside conventional cane crushing, and its distillery can run on molasses, sugarcane juice/syrup or grains, including production of Extra Neutral Alcohol (ENA).","products":{},"end_markets":{},"plants":{},"promoters":{},"board":{},"related":{},"strengths":{},"strategies":{},"expansion":"The AR does not disclose a named new capex/expansion project with a commissioning or ramp timeline. It describes an existing multi-feedstock distillery (335 KLPD total distillation capacity) with flexibility to run on molasses, sugarcane juice/syrup or grains, and the Punjab plant's ability to also produce Extra Neutral Alcohol (ENA), following modifications/modernisation carried out in the prior year that improved efficiency and margins in FY2025-26.","mdna":{},"risks":{},"as_of":"","concallIntel":{}},"topics":{"one_liner":{"title":"One Liner (RHP)","body":"An integrated Indian agri-processing company running sugar, ethanol/distillery and co-generation power operations across Punjab and Uttar Pradesh.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"business_model":{"title":"Business (RHP)","body":"Rana Sugars Limited manufactures crystal sugar, ethanol/spirit and co-generated power through three integrated manufacturing facilities in Uttar Pradesh (Moradabad, Rampur) and Punjab (Amritsar). It pioneered sugar-beet-based sugar manufacturing in India alongside conventional cane crushing, and its distillery can run on molasses, sugarcane juice/syrup or grains, including production of Extra Neutral Alcohol (ENA).","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"group_structure":{"title":"Related (RHP)","body":"[{\"name\": \"Kirandeep Kaur\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Daughter-in-law of Rana Ranjit Singh (Chairman/Promoter); holds a place of profit as Administration Head under Section 188(1)(f).\"}, {\"name\": \"Khushwinder Kumar & Co.\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Cost Accountants firm …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"end_markets":{"title":"End Markets (RHP)","body":"- Domestic Indian sugar market\n- Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) programme / Oil Marketing Companies\n- Punjab\n- Uttar Pradesh","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"certifications":{"title":"Certs (RHP)","body":"FSSAI certified (sugar units)","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"demand_drivers":{"title":"Mdna (RHP)","body":"- India's sugar production for SS2025-26 is estimated to rise ~18% over the prior season on favourable monsoon, better cane availability and improved recovery.\n- Government raised the Fair and Remunerative Price (FRP) of sugarcane to Rs 355/quintal for SS2025-26 from Rs 340/quintal, supporting farmer remuneration but raising input cost.\n- The Ethanol Blended Petrol (EBP) Programme continues to diversify sugar mill revenue streams and reduce dependence on cyclical sugar prices, with 20% blending (E20) achieved during FY2025-26.\n- Domestic sugar demand is expected to remain robust, driven by population …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"capex_expansion":{"title":"Expansion (RHP)","body":"The AR does not disclose a named new capex/expansion project with a commissioning or ramp timeline. It describes an existing multi-feedstock distillery (335 KLPD total distillation capacity) with flexibility to run on molasses, sugarcane juice/syrup or grains, and the Punjab plant's ability to also produce Extra Neutral Alcohol (ENA), following modifications/modernisation carried out in the prior year that improved efficiency and margins in FY2025-26.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"moat":{"title":"Strengths (RHP)","body":"- integration: Integrated sugar, ethanol and co-generation operations reduce cyclicality of the standalone sugar business — evidence: company operates three manufacturing facilities combining sugar, distillery and power co-generation, with the AR stating increased ethanol focus will help it 'beat the cyclical nature of business that the sugar industry has traditionally been associated with'\n- resource: Sole sugar-beet processing capability in India, diversifying feedstock beyond cane — evidence: 'India's only sugar beet processing facility at the Amritsar' unit, with sugar beet crushing capacity …","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- Government policies on FRP/SAP for sugarcane, sugar export regulations, domestic sales policy, ethanol procurement prices, blending programme and environmental regulations significantly impact operations and profitability.\n- Sugarcane production is influenced by rainfall patterns, temperature variations, drought, floods, pest infestation and crop diseases, which may affect cane availability, sugar recovery and operational efficiency.\n- Adequate quantity and quality of sugarcane directly impacts crushing operations and capacity utilisation.\n- Sugar prices are influenced by domestic demand-supply dynamics, inventory levels, export policies and international market trends; volatility may impact profitability.\n- The sugar industry requires substantial working capital due to seasonal procurement of sugarcane, inventory holding and statutory payment obligations.\n- Increasing environmental regulations on emissions, wastewater management, renewable energy and resource conservation require continuous compliance and investment.\n- Operational disruptions from equipment failure, plant shutdowns, accidents, fire or supply chain interruptions may adversely affect production.\n- The distillery segment's better margins are affected by volatility in raw material prices, especially grains, and government policies on FCI rice supply.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"strategy":{"title":"Strategies (RHP)","body":"- Deepen engagement with farmers, operate plants at optimal capacity and strengthen financial performance.\n- Introduce high-sugar-yielding cane varieties released by sugarcane breeding institutes to improve recovery.\n- Increase focus on ethanol to moderate the sugar segment's contribution and reduce cyclicality.\n- Mitigate regulatory and market risk by diversifying revenue through ethanol production and co-generation, and by improving operational efficiency and cost optimisation.","src":"drhp","as_of":""}},"scorecard":{"symbol":"RANASUG","fin_source":"shadow ledger (per-field legacy fallback)","fy_asof":"2026-03-31","opm_basis":"TTM 4q","opm_ttm":"1.25","roe":"0.46","roce":"3.65","bq_a":"0","sales_cagr_3y":"2.320765797101143","eps_cagr_3y":"-27.86205064883007","bq_b":"0","debt_equity":"0.5355790878012173","interest_cover":"2.2282241728561782","bq_c":"5","cfo_pat_3y":"2.2171059809417692","wc_basis":"WC/sales trend","bq_d":"10","share_cagr_3y":"4.440892098500626e-14","bq_e":"4","shp_asof":"2026-06-30","promoter_pct":"22.64","promoter_prev":"22.64","pledge_basis":"pledge not in snapshot -> 0 penalty (hook)","piotroski_basis":"needs 2 FYs of BS_* -> 0 (real from FY27)","bq_f":"2","g_integrity":"5","g_execution":"0","g_capalloc":"0","g_basis":"defaults (no WTT/ledger coverage)","bq_g":"5","bq_total":"26","bq_gate":"False","stage2":"False","sector_on":"False","market_on":"True","rs_rank":"